{%- comment -%}
  THE DIAMOND FEED AREA — the only part of /pages/diamonds that a provider
  replaces.

  ===========================================================================
  THE SEAM, AND WHY IT IS A BLOCK COUNT
  ===========================================================================
  This section accepts `@app` blocks. One branch:

      blocks present  -> render them. That IS the live feed.
      no blocks       -> render the Coming Soon state below.

  So connecting Nivoda, UNI or anyone else is one action in the theme editor:
  add their block to this section. The Coming Soon content then disappears on
  its own — nobody has to remember to remove it, which is exactly the kind of
  thing that gets forgotten and ends up stacked above a live product grid.
  Disconnecting a provider restores the Coming Soon state just as
  automatically.

  No template edit, no section swap, no URL change, no redesign of anything
  around it. The hero, shapes, pillars, four characteristics and ring path
  are separate sections and are untouched by the switch.

  WHY THE CONTROL PREVIEW LIVES IN THE COMING-SOON BRANCH and not above it:
  a connected provider brings its own filter UI. Two filter bars, one real
  and one decorative, is the worst outcome available here.

  ===========================================================================
  THE CONTROLS ARE INERT ON PURPOSE
  ===========================================================================
  The brief is explicit — the search presentation may be represented, but it
  must be clear live inventory is not connected, and placeholder filters must
  not appear operational.

  So the rail is wrapped in `inert`: no pointer events, no tab stops, no
  screen-reader exposure. It is framed and labelled "Preview" so the state
  reads as not-yet rather than broken, and `aria-hidden` keeps assistive
  technology from narrating eight controls that do nothing. The Coming Soon
  panel below it is the part that is real.

  NO FAKE INVENTORY. There are no diamond cards, no counts, no prices and no
  results grid anywhere in this file. A customer cannot be shown a stone that
  does not exist, and a reviewer cannot mistake a mock-up for stock.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'carat-diamonds.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign scheme = section.settings.color_scheme | default: 'scheme-1'
  assign anchor = section.settings.anchor_id | default: 'diamond-search'
-%}

<section id="{{ anchor }}" class="cd-feed color-{{ scheme }} gradient">
  <div class="page-width">
    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        LIVE. A provider's block is installed and owns this area entirely.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="cd-feed__live">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {% render block %}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

    {%- else -%}
      <div class="cd-head">
        <h2 class="cd-head__heading">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}</h2>
        {%- if section.settings.text != blank -%}
          <p class="cd-head__text">{{ section.settings.text | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <p class="cd-head__text" data-cd-context-holder hidden>
          {{ 'You asked about' }} <strong data-cd-context></strong> {{ 'diamonds. We will open that category first.' }}
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-preview cd-preview--spaced">
        <p class="cd-preview__tag">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7" />
            <path d="M16 16l5 5" />
          </svg>
          {{ section.settings.preview_label | escape }}
        </p>

        <div class="cd-preview__body">
          {%- comment -%}
            `inert` is the whole point of this wrapper. It is supported in
            every current browser and degrades to "looks dimmed, still
            unclickable because nothing is bound" in anything older.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="cd-rail" inert aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="cd-rail__row">
              <div class="cd-rail__group">
                <span class="cd-rail__label">Diamond type</span>
                <div class="cd-rail__toggle">
                  <span data-on="true">Lab-Grown</span>
                  <span>Natural</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="cd-rail__group">
                <span class="cd-rail__label">Shape</span>
                <div class="cd-rail__control">
                  <span>Any shape</span>
                  <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M2 4l4 4 4-4" /></svg>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="cd-rail__group">
                <span class="cd-rail__label">Certification</span>
                <div class="cd-rail__control">
                  <span>Any laboratory</span>
                  <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M2 4l4 4 4-4" /></svg>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="cd-rail__row">
              <div class="cd-rail__group">
                <span class="cd-rail__label">Carat</span>
                <div class="cd-rail__track"><i></i></div>
              </div>
              <div class="cd-rail__group">
                <span class="cd-rail__label">Price</span>
                <div class="cd-rail__track"><i></i></div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="cd-rail__row">
              <div class="cd-rail__group">
                <span class="cd-rail__label">Cut</span>
                <div class="cd-rail__track"><i></i></div>
              </div>
              <div class="cd-rail__group">
                <span class="cd-rail__label">Colour</span>
                <div class="cd-rail__track"><i></i></div>
              </div>
              <div class="cd-rail__group">
                <span class="cd-rail__label">Clarity</span>
                <div class="cd-rail__track"><i></i></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cd-soon">
          {%- comment -%} A drawn brilliant-cut outline, not a photograph. {%- endcomment -%}
          <svg class="cd-soon__mark" width="34" height="34" viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M10 18h28L24 40z" />
            <path d="M10 18l5-10h18l5 10" />
            <path d="M15 8l4 10M33 8l-4 10M10 18h28" />
          </svg>

          <h3 class="cd-soon__title">{{ section.settings.soon_heading | escape }}</h3>

          {%- if section.settings.soon_text != blank -%}
            <p class="cd-soon__text">{{ section.settings.soon_text | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.soon_cta_label != blank -%}
            <div class="cd-soon__actions">
              <a class="button" href="{{ section.settings.soon_cta_link | default: '/pages/first-access' }}">
                {{- section.settings.soon_cta_label | escape -}}
              </a>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.soon_note != blank -%}
            <p class="cd-soon__note">{{ section.settings.soon_note | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Carat diamond feed",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Add a diamond provider's app block here to go live. The Coming Soon state below is shown only while there is no block, and disappears by itself once one is added."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "anchor_id",
      "label": "Anchor id",
      "default": "diamond-search",
      "info": "Linked to from the hero and the homepage. Changing it breaks those links."
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Colour scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Shown only before a provider is connected" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Search the diamond marketplace" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "text",
      "label": "Supporting copy",
      "default": "These are the controls you will use to narrow an extensive certified inventory down to the one stone you want."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "preview_label",
      "label": "Preview frame label",
      "default": "Preview — live inventory is not connected yet"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "soon_heading",
      "label": "Coming Soon heading",
      "default": "Diamond Marketplace Coming Soon"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "soon_text",
      "label": "Coming Soon copy",
      "default": "We're preparing direct access to an extensive selection of certified natural and lab-grown diamonds. Soon you'll be able to compare diamonds, certificates and pricing in one place."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "soon_cta_label", "label": "Button", "default": "Join the Early Access List" },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "soon_cta_link",
      "label": "Button link",
      "info": "Defaults to /pages/first-access — the existing First Access signup, which already offers a Loose Diamonds interest. A `url` setting cannot carry a relative default in its schema (Shopify rejects the section outright), so the fallback lives in this section's Liquid instead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "soon_note",
      "label": "Small note",
      "default": "First Access members hear before the public launch."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [{ "type": "@app" }],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Carat diamond feed" }]
}
{% endschema %}
